<title>USA: Racing-car stocks may have some kick -- Barron's.</title>
<headline>Racing-car stocks may have some kick -- Barron's.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-03-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares of race-car stocks and racing companies may rise because of fast-growing audiences for racing, increased television dollars and sponsorship, Barron's said.</p>
<p>The racing car industry can also raise profits by adding seats, putting on extra racing events and raising the fees they get from TV, the magazine said, adding that &quot;race tracks are selling out events and television ratings are leaving other sports in the dust.&quot;</p>
<p>The magazine recommended the following racing stocks:</p>
<p>Dover Downs Entertainment Inc</p>
<p>Grand Prix Association of Long Beach</p>
<p>International Speedway Corp</p>
<p>Penske Motorsports Inc</p>
<p>Speedway Motorsports Inc</p>
</text>
